<title>FRANCE: 1997 FRENCH BUDGET - Spending by government area.</title>
<headline>1997 FRENCH BUDGET - Spending by government area.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French government released the following department-by-department breakdown for spending in 1997. The 1996 comparisons refer to the revised figures issued in June's mini-budget. (Spending figures in millions of francs)</p>
<p> SPENDING AREA			 1996	 1997    Pct change</p>
<p>Foreign Affairs and Cooperation</p>
<p>   - Foreign Affairs		15,034     14,438	 -4.0</p>
<p>   - Cooperation		     7,287	6,720	 -7.8</p>
<p> Agriculture, Fish and Food     35,505     35,222	 -0.8</p>
<p>Regional Development, Towns and Integration</p>
<p>   - Regional development	  1,976	1,670	-15.5</p>
<p>   - Towns			     1,358	1,287	 -5.3</p>
<p> War veterans and victims	 28,367     26,842	 -5.4</p>
<p> Shared Departmental Expenses  364,214    374,278	  2.8</p>
<p> Commerce and Crafts		   516	  436	-15.6</p>
<p> Culture				15,532     15,077	 -2.9</p>
<p>Education</p>
<p>   - Schools			 273,144    277,193	  1.5</p>
<p>   - Higher education	     44,572     47,001	  5.4</p>
<p>   - Research			 28,858     28,905	  0.2</p>
<p> Environment			   1,758	1,861	  5.9</p>
<p>Equipment, Housing, Transport and Tourism</p>
<p>   - Urban Affairs		  22,794     22,639	 -0.7</p>
<p>- Transport</p>
<p>     - Ground transport	   44,565     44,542	 -0.1</p>
<p>     - Roads			   7,784	7,307	 -6.1</p>
<p>     - Road safety		     500	  430	-14.0</p>
<p>     - Air			     1,382	  978	-29.2</p>
<p>     - Meteorology		   1,193	1,161	 -2.7</p>
<p>   - Housing			  42,152     40,323	 -4.3</p>
<p>   - Maritime			  6,291	6,215	 -1.2</p>
<p>   - Tourism			     399	  350	-12.2</p>
<p>Industry Post &amp; Telecommunications</p>
<p>  - Industry			  16,968     14,139	-16.7</p>
<p>  - Post Telecoms &amp; Space	 10,335     11,017	  6.6</p>
<p> Interior and Decentralisation  78,518     75,701	 -3.6</p>
<p> Youth and Sports		    2,998	2,929	 -2.3</p>
<p> Justice				23,477     23,892	  1.8</p>
<p> Overseas Territories		4,859	4,862	  0.1</p>
<p>Prime Minister's Office</p>
<p>   - General Services		4,404	4,016	 -8.8</p>
<p>   - National Defence		  201	  141	-30.2</p>
<p>   - Economic			    169	  178	  5.8</p>
<p>   - Plan				  161	  150	 -6.6</p>
<p> Financial Services		 45,667     45,849	  0.4</p>
<p>Labour and Social Affairs</p>
<p>   - Labour			   99,464    102,977	  3.5</p>
<p>   - Public Health		   8,240	8,116	 -1.5</p>
<p>   - Social Action, Solidarity  59,226     61,424	  3.7</p>
<p> TOTAL CIVIL BUDGET	    1,299,865  1,310,266	  0.8</p>
<p> Defence			     241,448    243,338	  0.8</p>
<p> TOTAL GENERAL BUDGET	  1,541,314  1,553,604	  0.8</p>
<p> Special Treasury Accounts	10,655	 -699	  N/A</p>
<p> TOTAL NET EXPENSES	    1,551,969  1,552,905	 0.06</p>
<p>NOTE: Shared departmental expenses take account of the transfer of France Telecom funds. The government said housing spending rose 2.8 percent taking account of special Treasury accounts credits.</p>
